      "arabic_text": "أُولٰئِكَ يُؤْتَوْنَ أَجْرَهُم مَّرَّتَيْنِ بِمَا صَبَرُوا وَيَدْرَءُونَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ السَّيِّئةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنَاهُمْ يُنفِقُونَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Those will be given their recompense twice, for they persevered and repelled evil with good, and spent of what We had given them."
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This verse describes the reward for those who combine patience with active goodness and charity. They receive a double reward: one for their steadfastness (sabr) and another for their ability to neutralize evil with good deeds, as well as for their financial generosity.",
      "seo_question": "in the way of God."
